# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the AQIB-FILM portfolio website.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Documentation Review
- Fetched the latest official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Identified that this is a React + Vite project based on the package.json and project structure
- Followed the React-specific installation instructions from the official docs

### 2. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using pnpm (the project's package manager)
- Package successfully added to dependencies in package.json
- Lock file (pnpm-lock.yaml) updated with new dependency

### 3. Code Integration
**Modified: src/App.tsx**
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the main App component's return statement
- Component placed after Footer, ensuring it loads on all pages

### 4. Code Quality
**Modified files (formatted by oxfmt):**
- src/App.tsx - Added SpeedInsights import and component
- src/main.tsx - Quote style formatting changes
- vite.config.ts - Quote style formatting changes

The formatter (oxfmt) also made cosmetic changes (single quotes to double quotes) to maintain consistent code style across the project.

### 5. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully (vite build)
- ✅ Code formatter ran without errors (oxfmt)
- ✅ No TypeScript compilation errors
- ✅ Production bundle generated successfully
- ✅ Lock file properly updated

## Files Changed
1. **package.json** - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
2. **pnpm-lock.yaml** - Updated with new dependency resolution
3. **src/App.tsx** - Added SpeedInsights import and component
4. **src/main.tsx** - Formatted by oxfmt
5. **vite.config.ts** - Formatted by oxfmt

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab
3. No additional configuration is required - the component works out of the box
4. Real User Monitoring (RUM) data will be collected from actual visitors

## Technical Notes
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and won't impact page performance
- It automatically tracks Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics
- Works seamlessly with React's rendering lifecycle
- No API keys or manual configuration required when deployed on Vercel
